## ============================================================
## SCRIPT 1 — Antigens as outcomes (SENSITIVITY) — LEFT-CENSORED
## WITHIN-SITE GRAVIDITY CONTRASTS
##
## Identical to the automated-screening script. The ONLY change is
## which contrasts are estimated:
##
##   before: Primi anchored against every other group, 12 contrasts
##           per marker, mixing within-site and cross-site comparisons
##
##   now:    primigravidae vs multigravidae WITHIN each site,
##           3 contrasts per marker
##
## WHY (reviewer point 7)
##   Site and gravidity are confounded, so a cross-site contrast
##   mixes the gravidity effect with everything else that differs
##   between sites. Comparing primigravidae with multigravidae inside
##   the same site holds all of that constant.
##
##   It also costs far less multiplicity: Sidak across 3 contrasts
##   uses a threshold of about 0.017; across 12 it was about 0.0043.
##
## EVERYTHING ELSE IS UNCHANGED
##   - values below the LLOQ are LEFT-CENSORED, not dropped and not
##     set to zero (reviewer points 2 and 3)
##   - all qPCR-positive infections enter, no detectability filter
##   - automated LRT screening of HIV x density and gestweeks x
##     density; the three-way density x gravidity x site term is
##     retained a priori because it is the primary hypothesis
##   - cubic-spline refit of the selected structure (point 6)
##   - SIMULTANEOUS 95% confidence bands across the density curve
##     (point 5)
##
## THREE FIXES relative to the version this came from
##   1) nobs() replaced by nrow(model.frame()); survreg has no nobs
##      method and the default returns the wrong number
##   2) MASS loaded by namespace only; attaching it would mask
##      dplyr::select and break every select() downstream
##   3) net / fumig left as they arrive from the recoding script,
##      where 999 was already merged into "yes"
## ============================================================

